course: dictionary
lesson: 2885
title: Dope: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Dope is a good example. The context, meaning the words around it, shows you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: In sport, dope means a banned drug taken to cheat. «Lance Armstrong won the Tour de France seven times and lost all seven titles in 2012 for doping.» The clues are banned, cheat and lost titles, so doping must mean taking banned drugs to race faster.
explain: Between friends, dope can be a teasing word for a silly person, as in «You dope, you left your bag on the bus again!» Put silly in place of dope and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Dope can also be slang for great or cool, and it can mean inside information about something. Read the whole sentence before you choose a meaning.
fact: Dope has several meanings, so the context tells you which one is meant.
fact: A dope is a silly or foolish person. This is informal, so use it only when you are teasing a friend.
fact: Dope is also slang for an illegal drug. Drugs can seriously harm your body, so never take any drug or medicine unless a grown-up you trust gives it to you.
fact: Doping means giving drugs to an athlete or animal to cheat in sport. It is against the rules, and drug tests can catch it.
fact: The dope on something means the inside information about it, such as the dope on the new game.
exercise: «You dope, you left your bag on the bus again!» What does dope mean here? | Something very cool | A winner's medal | A drug | *A silly or foolish person
exercise: «Lance Armstrong lost all seven titles in 2012 for doping.» What does doping mean? | Running a fast race in the rain | Training with a coach every day | Eating a big breakfast before a race | *Taking banned drugs to race faster
exercise: Ana says, «That new game is dope!» What does dope mean here? | Very boring | Full of illegal drugs | A silly person | *Really great or cool
test: «Lance Armstrong lost all seven titles in 2012 for doping.» Why was doping wrong? | It was too expensive to do | It made the race too short | It was against the rules to wear a helmet | *It was cheating by using banned drugs
test: Sam says, «The dope on the new phone is that it has a huge battery.» What does dope mean here? | A cheap phone | A phone that plays music | *The inside information about it | A broken phone
exam: Jayden asks, «How do I know which meaning of dope the writer wants?» What is the best answer? | Skip the word and never think about it again | Always pick the first meaning you see in a dictionary | Guess at random and move on | *Read the words around it, then try each meaning in the sentence
